hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  video I'm going to answer a question  from one of our readers Nicolas who says  thanks a lot for the inspirational  quotes just to ask one question what are  the risks in small-scale  entrepreneurship and how do we as  entrepreneurs manage them for the  purposes of our business sustainability  good day Nicolas so Nicolas I think the  biggest risks that entrepreneurs face  when they're launching their business is  losing everything and a lot of  entrepreneurs will sell out all their  savings and take on additional debt and  you know market to their home and their  business doesn't work out they're really  left without anything I have to start  all over again so that's a pretty huge  risk and I want to make sure that you  guys don't have to face that and a few  ideas to you that hopefully will help so  the first is you don't have to start  your business on a full-time basis it's  start card time and what that does is  give you money from your current job and  allows you to build your business up  over time and hopefully you're in a job  that you can learn some skills or meet  some people that will eventually help  your business grow as well and it's  important that you take steps every day  to grow your business so it's not just  spending three months going crazy  full-time and then you run out of money  you have to go get a job you'll do  better and spending a little bit of time  every day over a longer period of time  so you let that moment and grow and  allows your business to flourish the  second thing I would encourage you to do  is try to build around a customer a lot  of entrepreneurs start with a great idea  that think it's gonna change the world  and then they go out and try to sell it  and nobody wants fire so try to start  the other way around try to start by  finding customers who have a problem and  are willing to pay for a solution for it  if you can find those people it's the  best way to build a business because you  have money coming in right away and  reduce  the risk of you run out of money having  to close down your business so try as  much as you can to find a paying  customer to start the last thing that I  would recommend is try not to spend  money until you're making money and that  might sound like common sense but a lot  of entrepreneurs do the exact opposite  where they start a business and invest  tons of money now go get an office you  might need a car for the business you  make up all these expenses that you  think you need but in reality try not to  spend anything until you have money  coming in you may need business cards  and a simple simple website but that's  it the rest is what equity is your time  going now trying to find business and  try not to start spending money because  you'll often spend it on the wrong  things until you have money coming in  and once you have that money coming in  you know what's working and you can  spend money to amplify those results so  I hope that helps if you guys like the  video please give it a thumbs up below  and I'll make more  and I'd also love to hear thoughts and  feedback if you want to leave a comment  and stay tuned for the next episode  you
 

